## What the patch is
A byte-exact FORWARD `git show 05cfd1b -- triggarr/web/routes.py`. It ADDS the
already-shipped, clean settings-handler half of the drain-timeout feature: imports
`safe_float`, renders `shutdown_drain_timeout` in the GET context dict adjacent to
`max_consecutive_failures`, and parses the POSTed value via
`safe_float(form.get("shutdown_drain_timeout"), 60.0, 1.0, 3600.0)` — a bounded,
default-clamped parse mirroring the existing `safe_int` parses beside it. This is
defect-free feature code — reviewing it should produce NO critical/warning
finding. Safe ON the settings input-parse path: user form input flows only through
the bounded safe_float helper (default 60.0, floor 1.0, ceiling 3600.0); no raw
interpolation, no injection surface, no resource issue.

